{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/fixtures/globe/globe.html","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T19:46:24.371092Z","id":"94b0041579be1ab04dd7c5d01afc912347494bcd7a74fbd858e641b9d7f6aeea","body":{"detail":"The camera's frames end at REEL_EPOCH + a multiple of 2000 ms (ROLL_GRID_MS) + round(k*1000/30), and requestAnimationFrame ticks every 16 ms, so every 400 ms an animation frame falls exactly on a frame's end and the screenshot sometimes caught the canvas before that draw: two recordings differed at those frames. tick() maps any time to the end of its 30 fps frame, so every draw within one camera frame draws the same picture. Off camera this only caps the globe at 30 fps. If the camera's grid or rate changes, this page needs the same change.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":296},"end":{"line":307},"content_hash":"4baf9e7d496a11ac943b29f86ec171006253e9d493af202bf366b945419e1dc7"},"summary":"The globe draws on 30 fps frames aligned to two-second spans of the wall clock, matching the deterministic camera's frame grid","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
